{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You were admitted last night with worsening abdominal pain. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, yes. The pain started again in my upper belly, right under the ribs, and it’s spreading to the right side. It’s a burning feeling, worse than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned this has happened a few times recently. Are you having nausea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been nauseous and dry heaving. I haven’t eaten much the last day. I’m still doing tube feeds, but they don’t seem to bother me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fevers, chills, or changes in bowel movements?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fevers. I had one loose stool yesterday, but this morning it was normal. I’m worried it might be another ulcer or maybe a stitch left behind from surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a possibility. We’ve reviewed your CT scan from last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And? Did you see anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan shows no abscess, infection, or blockage. Your gallbladder, liver, and pancreas look normal. The gastrostomy tube is in the right place. No signs of a new ulcer or perforation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why does it hurt so much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t have a clear cause yet. But your pain could be related to inflammation or nerve sensitivity near the surgical site. Your labs are mostly normal—no infection or organ issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking acetaminophen at home, but it’s not helping much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to start you on oxycodone every four hours for better pain control. We also want to increase your free water flushes through the tube to 100 mL every four hours. Dehydration can make pain worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been doing 60 mL three times a day. Is more water safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s safe and should help keep you hydrated. We’ll monitor your electrolytes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about long-term? I can’t keep coming back every few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re starting gabapentin, which helps with nerve-related pain. It may take a few days to work. You’ll follow up with the pain clinic after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Gabapentin? I’ve heard of that. Is it safe with my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s safe. We checked for interactions. We’re keeping all your usual meds—sucralfate, PPI, rifaximin, and your fluoxetine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve also noticed a little leaking around my G-tube site. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked this morning. No redness or infection. A small amount of leakage can happen. Just keep the area clean and dry. Use the mupirocin ointment as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-04-26 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, actually. The pain is still there, but not as sharp. The new meds might be helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We gave you a nutritional supplement through the tube yesterday to make sure you’re getting enough calories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel any discomfort from it. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s well tolerated. Your labs this morning are looking good—white blood cell count is normal, and no signs of dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I might be able to go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We want to make sure your pain is stable on oral meds and you’re tolerating your regular tube feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-04-27 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I just want to get back to my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your medications, including the new gabapentin three times a day and oxycodone every six hours as needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need a prescription for those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll get a six-week supply. Also, keep doing 100 mL water flushes every four hours. Watch for fever, vomiting, or worsening pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the pain gets bad again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Try the oxycodone first. If it doesn’t help within a few hours, or if you develop new symptoms, come back or call your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have follow-up with my surgeon and primary care. Should I mention the gabapentin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and you’re scheduled with the pain clinic next week. They may adjust the dose if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get the discharge papers ready. You should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I avoid any foods or activities?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No specific food restrictions. Just continue your regular tube feeding formula. Avoid heavy lifting for now, and listen to your body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Just keep up with your care plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly with your prescriptions and discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-04-28 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-04-26 08:44:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-04-28 16:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for worsening epigastric abdominal pain radiating to the right upper quadrant, following a recent discharge for similar symptoms. With a history of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and gastrostomy tube placement due to prior anastomotic ulcer, she presented with burning pain, nausea, and decreased oral intake. A CT scan showed no acute intra-abdominal abnormality, abscess, or obstruction. Pain was managed with oxycodone and gabapentin, and hydration was optimized by increasing free water flushes to 100 mL every four hours. Her condition improved, and she was discharged home on oral pain medications with plans for follow-up in the pain clinic. She remained on her chronic medications for depression, anxiety, anemia, and hyperlipidemia, with no complications during the stay.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified mood [affective] disorder",
      "Polycystic ovarian syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
